o be on  to discuss her vision for castle rocks  revitalization at Molly's new office  Molly places the finishing touches on  her diorama and we learned Jackie has  taken on the job of Molly's Executive  Assistant  Molly senses the arrival of Henry who  has plans to sell her mother's home and  put her in extended care he says he  needs an agent but Molly refuses to take  him on the voices in her head are too  much and she makes a pitiful excuse that  she's too busy in a flashback Henry  Burns of VHS  with the date November 23rd 1989 he's  also wearing the same plaid shirt Molly  took before killing father Deaver and  now remains in her basement as it burns  he expresses his hatred for his dad  implying that whatever was on that tape  was important to him in some way could  it be something he wasn't allowed to  watch that a pastor wouldn't want their  kid watching like porn since Molly says  she could feel him touch himself or  could it be video of his real family my  guess is this won't be the last time we  see this video molly invites henry over  where you can see the notepad from  episode two judging by the cassette  tapes this is the summer of 1990 a few  months prior to henry's disappearance  you can also make out a poster for the  Ramones who wrote a single for the film  Pet Sematary Molly tells Henry that she  can feel what he feels and we see this  manifested itself when Henry's father  angrily calls for him and she curls her  fist just like he does back in present  day Molly takes her last pill in an  effort to cope with the voices at  Shawshank the kid eats nothing but bread  for lunch he stares at the photo of de  Lacey the man who imprisoned him in the  water tank who also happens to be next  to a picture of warden Norton from the  Shawshank Redemption so les key tells  him to keep it cool and that Henry is  arranged for a hearing with his case  Henry meets with Zaleski who tells him  he needs more proof if he's going to get  the kid out Molly comes home 