ail  and she opens up about why she can't be  around him she tells him she loses track  of herself with him could this mean she  was acting out Henry's anger when she  pulled the plug from his father all  those years ago does she have some form  of The Shining which might play out  later since her new assistant just  happens to be someone named Jackie  Torrence  Henry rushes Molly to her interview  where she experiences an influx of  voices but watches it when she uses her  time to talk about the injustice of the  kid being locked up at Shawshank without  due process much to the awe of warden  Porter Molly drives Henry home and they  both say it was good to see each other  before Henry gets a call from Shawshank  warden Porter meets with Henry and  offers a three hundred thousand dollar  settlement for the kid Henry argues that  won't cut it this was a kidnapping but  Porter says they can't be held  responsible for the actions of a rogue  employee  de Lacey Henry and the kid meet face to  face the kid doesn't seem to know how to  use a phone which supports my theory  that he isn't from this time or place  remember how scared he was of the  electronic fingerprint scanner in  Episode one the kid asked if it has  begun  could he be referring to the war between  good and evil and later asks do you hear  it now just like his father asked 27  years ago now there's a theory out there  that the kid is Georgie from it because  of the line about boats and it being 27  years the difference the same amount of  time it takes for it to reappear but I'm  not quite sold on that the line about  boats that makes me think of no in the  great flood and with all this talk about  the end of days  the second coming in Corinthians not to  mention the kid being found in a water  tank I'm more inclined to think the kid  is a messenger from God that Alan  Pangborn and de Lacy have sworn to  protect if you think about it the only  bad thing the kid has done so far which  even that can't be con